                <pb facs="1129" n="954" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v10-12mSupp/pg954"/>

                <head>284. Memorandum for the record, May 17<anchor n="1" xml:id="d284-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head" calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1962-05-17">May 17, 1962</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d284-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d284-1"/>
                <p rendition="#section-heading #italic">Memorandum of Review of Operation
                    Mongoose—Thursday, May 17th</p>
                <p>General Lansdale reported on the
                    operations, submitting a written statement of even date covering operations from
                    May 11th to 17th.</p>
                <p>There was no discussion of Mr. Harvey’s
                    report on TV intrusions of May 16th except to the extent commented in the
                        Lansdale report.</p>
                <p>General Lansdale submitted a new
                    schedule of priority operations for the period May 21st to June 30th. The
                    schedule was accepted by the Special Group for review and study and decision at
                    the meeting on Thursday, May 24th.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed corresp="#p_MJA_1">John A.
                            McCone</signed>
                    <affiliation>Director</affiliation>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
